{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789902527,"nonce":"itiV0XJfQ5J2eMHQY7HawWgQI2A=","message":"Fixed in 61e0fa7755f7559ff9d7c6eb59dc22228989e1ef. Root cause as described: compiled frames left nothing for the trace, and a runtime error raised from a native helper reported after its frames had unwound (no span, no trace at all, in every mode). Now: compiled bodies keep a frame record (prev, func_id|site) linked from JitThread::frame_head, written before each call that can raise; interpreter frames note the head at push; the trace interleaves both; errors capture their site at the raise. Reproducer (abort 3M iterations into a tiered loop) went from label on the caller loop line + missing frames to the abort line with boom/run/module and line numbers, in tiered, cranelift-only, early-LLVM and hot-threshold modes; e2e_trace_through_compiled_frames covers it. Cost on the NUC: binary_trees ~+10% (the prologue on the recursive check), dyn_dispatch/method_call within noise; a zero-cost frame-pointer walk with return-address tables is filed separately. Remaining cosmetic gap: the diagnostic header prints \u003cunknown\u003e for the module name (ariadne source is unnamed), pre-existing.","files":null}]}